        {[
          { q: "How do I respond when a brand asks me to name my price first?", a: "Name it. The first number shapes the negotiation, so you want to set the anchor. State your rate clearly and confidently: 'My standard rate for a 30–60 second UGC video with one revision round is $X.' If you are uncomfortable picking a single number, present three tiered options. Never deflect with 'what's your budget?' — that hands the anchor to the other side." },
          { q: "Should I negotiate on price or scope?", a: "Scope first, price second. If a brand cannot meet your rate, ask what deliverables you can adjust: fewer revision rounds, shorter video length, raw footage instead of edited. Reducing scope preserves your per-hour rate while giving the brand a way to work within their budget. Only reduce price if the scope stays the same and the brand offers something valuable in return — guaranteed volume, long-term contract, or usage rights that benefit you." },
          { q: "What if I already quoted a low rate and want to raise it with an existing client?", a: "Be direct. Send a message 30 days before the next project: 'Starting next month, my rate for this type of content will be $X. This reflects my updated portfolio and current market rates.' Do not apologize or over-explain. If the client pushes back, offer to honor the old rate for one final project as a transition. Most clients who value your work will accept a reasonable increase." },
          { q: "Is it unprofessional to decline a project because the pay is too low?", a: "No. It is unprofessional to accept a rate you resent, deliver mediocre work because you are unmotivated, and create a strained relationship where neither side is satisfied. Declining politely and recommending another creator at a lower price point is one of the most professional things you can do. It protects your standards and helps the brand find the right fit." },
          { q: "Can OKAD help me set my rates and find brand deals?", a: "Yes. We manage pricing, negotiations, and brand relationships for our creator network. If you are a UGC creator looking for consistent work at fair rates, reach out at olga@okad.agency. We handle the business side so you can focus on creating." },
